\paragraph{Cross-Architecture L1 Instruction Dominance}
Figure~\ref{fig:cross_arch_l1_bar} complements the main-text summary (Figure~\ref{fig:cross_arch_l1}) by showing the fraction of instruction-dominant heads at L1 across all three architectures in a single comparison. The trained/reference fractions are comparable within each architecture (OpenVLA: 23/32 vs.\ 26/32; TraceVLA: 27/32 vs.\ 32/32; NORA: 13/16 vs.\ 13/16), consistent with L1 instruction attention being largely inherited from the pretrained backbone rather than acquired during VLA fine-tuning.

